      "rev_n_6_9742dd_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_9742dd_1",
        "node_id": "n_6_9742dd",
        "thought_text": "The error in the previous reasoning was that it didn't account for the possibility of multiple box passes within the 3-minute window. The correct approach should be to keep track of the total time elapsed and only move the box when the time reaches or exceeds 3 minutes and 30 seconds. This ensures that the box is passed to the next player at the correct moment, regardless of the time taken to answer the previous question. Additionally, the loop should continue until the total time reaches or exceeds 210 seconds, not just when it's less than 210 seconds.",
